      "problem": "The identifying chain requires confirming that U_KENJI holds a second workspace membership in 'Product Beta' via users.info. The domain's runtime_qualifications state that users.info exposes only 'one selected workspace association' per user and recommends giving each queried person a single workspace membership for reproducible profile predicates. The design instead requires U_KENJI to hold two memberships (main workspace + Product Beta) and relies on users.info to surface the Product Beta one specifically for him while other reactors (single-membership) are correctly excluded. No scope_exception is declared to explain how the actor's session/scope reliably resolves to the Product Beta association rather than the primary one, so the discovery step described in access_plan is not clearly supported by the documented API behavior.",
      "repair": "Add an explicit scope_exception describing how the actor's session is scoped (e.g., actor holds membership across all workspaces and can select Product Beta context when calling users.info) so the membership check is deterministically discoverable, or restructure the identifying condition to avoid depending on an ambiguous 'one selected workspace' field."
